<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicolás Maduro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nicolás Maduro is a Venezuelan politician, a former bus driver and trade unionist who served as foreign minister under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugo-chavez">Hugo Chávez</a> and succeeded him as president in 2013. His rule saw economic collapse, hyperinflation and the emigration of millions, while disputed elections in 2018 and 2024 were widely rejected abroad. In January 2026 he was seized by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracas">Caracas</a> and taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> to face trial.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicolas-maduro.jpg" alt="Nicolás Maduro" width="320" height="433" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Presidency of Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicol%C3%A1s_Maduro_official_portrait_(cropped_2).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
